# Payment Webhook Event
# Example Business Knowledge expressed in Menata Language
# Domain: Payments — the raw inbound notification, received and deduplicated before
# any domain processing happens ("receive fast, process safe")
# Case 8 of the Case Portfolio (runtime/case-portfolio.md)
# Grounded in webhook idempotency practice: every provider delivers at-least-once,
# so duplicates are part of the contract, not an edge case. Dedupe key = the
# provider's own event ID; the check-and-claim must be one atomic operation.

Payment Webhook Event

Fields

- Provider Event ID : Text
- Provider : Bank Transfer | Payment Gateway
- Raw Payload : Rich Text
- Received At : Date Time
- Processing Status : Received | Processed | Duplicate | Failed

Events

When Receive

    if Provider Event ID already exists among Payment Webhook Event

        Processing Status Duplicate

    Received At Now

    Create Payment

    Processing Status Processed

Constraints

- Provider Event ID is required.
- Provider is required.

Permissions

System

- Receive

Views

- Event List : List
- Duplicate Events : List
- Event Detail : Detail
